\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Positioning against federated LoRA and client-selection systems. \checkmark  {} = the property holds in the cited papers' own descriptions; $\times $ = absent or not reported. Delivery-aware means that a scheduling or adaptation decision conditions on per-round network delivery state (rate, deadline, delivery probability) rather than on training progress, device capability, or static profiling alone. Real payload means payload is accounted as transmitted bytes rather than a fixed or parameter-count proxy. Real training means model training is executed in the evaluation as reported.}}{3}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
