\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The FedRAS architecture. Action Construction (AC) scores every client--rank pair with the delivery hazard \cref  {eq:hazard} and the saturating capacity \cref  {eq:cap}; the GridDP assignment (GDP) computes the client--rank assignment under the byte budget and the admission cap. Updates arriving within the deadline $\tau $ pass the on-time gate and are merged by Masked Aggregation (MA) while the shared factor $A$ stays frozen; observed outcomes update the link-state history. AC, GDP, and MA correspond to \cref  {alg:ac,alg:gdp,alg:ma}; the overall round is \cref  {alg:fedras}.}}{4}{figure.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{4}{The FedRAS architecture. Action Construction (AC) scores every client--rank pair with the delivery hazard \cref {eq:hazard} and the saturating capacity \cref {eq:cap}; the GridDP assignment (GDP) computes the client--rank assignment under the byte budget and the admission cap. Updates arriving within the deadline $\tau $ pass the on-time gate and are merged by Masked Aggregation (MA) while the shared factor $A$ stays frozen; observed outcomes update the link-state history. AC, GDP, and MA correspond to \cref {alg:ac,alg:gdp,alg:ma}; the overall round is \cref {alg:fedras}}{figure.11}{}}
\newlabel{fig:architecture@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][3][]4}}
